  {
    "id": 3948779792,
    "type": null,
    "body": "Two cases from MR !17's second review round (2026-10-03) belong here.\n\n**A trade COMMIT that goes unanswered** (MariaDB client error 2013) is now settled in\n`trade_record()` (fix `2ba35d6b1`, on `feat/vessels-s12` / MR !18): the trade's writes set absolute\nvalues, so it is written again on a reconnected session, and the second commit decides the\noutcome. What remains: if that second write cannot commit either (the database unreachable just\nafter a lost reply), the database may not match the ship's hold until her manifest is next written\nand the minute save runs. A reload before then lets the database's version win. A settlement\nrecord would close this.\n\n**Freight acceptance** (`do_contractaccept()`, `src/vessels/vessels_contracts.c`) has the same\nCOMMIT shape: an unanswered COMMIT unloads the freight and reports \"no gold was taken\" even if the\ncontract was taken and the freight stowed. Its write is conditional\n(`UPDATE ... WHERE status = OPEN`), so it cannot simply be repeated: writing it again after a\ncommit that did land finds the contract taken and reports another captain. The settlement record\nplanned here (a durable intent the reconcile can find) is the fix; dock-fee payment should get the\nsame check.",
    "author": {
      "id": 42759441,
      "username": "max757",
      "public_email": "",
      "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
      "state": "active",
      "locked": false,
      "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/max757"
    },
    "created_at": "2026-10-03T07:13:58.992Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-03T07:13:58.992Z",
