  {
    "id": 3949791084,
    "type": null,
    "body": "Scheduled as **S14** of the vessel study, resolved in the `../Luminari-Source-vessels-ships` worktree after S13 (#13):\n\n- Branch: `feat/vessels-s14`, to be cut from S13's merge commit with the annotated tag `vessels-s14-base`.\n- Plan and record: [`docs/ongoing-projects/vessels-ships.md`](https://gitlab.com/max757/Luminari-Source/-/blob/feat/vessels-s13/docs/ongoing-projects/vessels-ships.md#part-5-implementation-sequence), Part 5 item 14 (commit b15a8bc607e6ba03f9518ac7ff6465e1488abf72): the settlement table is schema Phase 25, and the player-file marker follows the two the vessel code already keeps (`VIns` for insurance claims, `VMer` for merchant consequences), with the reconcile beside their login deliveries (`src/core/interpreter.c`).\n- Scope, as described above: `cargobuy`, `cargosell`, `contractaccept` and `dockfees pay`. The settlement row is also the durable marker that settles an unanswered `COMMIT` for them, which S13 (#13) leaves to this step.\n- Order: S13 comes first because this step uses its shared `COMMIT` helper (committed, refused or unanswered) and its rule that a connection that lost its transaction accepts nothing but `ROLLBACK`.\n- The S14 merge request will say `Closes #12`, so it is listed here and closes this item when it merges.\n\nNot started yet.",
    "author": {
      "id": 42759441,
      "username": "max757",
      "public_email": "",
      "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
      "state": "active",
      "locked": false,
      "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
